cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
title: "Horizon: Closing the loop on frozen flow-matching VLAs"
abstract: >-
  Horizon studies the open-loop execution gap in frozen flow-matching
  vision-language-action policies. A frozen SmolVLA action expert executes
  50-step action chunks open-loop on MetaWorld; shrinking the execution horizon
  (replanning more often, i.e. closing the loop) yields large paired success
  gains. The repository curates the faithful evaluation harness, the falsified
  swings (CASTLE, STL-GDPA, NIAC averaging, dispersion-predicts-failure), and
  the positive open-loop-gap evidence that motivates a trained, compute-efficient
  closed-loop method.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "lexus-x / Horizon project"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-05-30"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - vision-language-action
  - flow-matching
  - SmolVLA
  - MetaWorld
  - closed-loop control
  - open-loop execution gap
